IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 5, 5A and 5B: gaming and wagering contracts, maintenance and champerty, third-party funding.
--
-- Section 5(1) and (2) state a nullity and a bar; subsections (3) to (5) lift them for listed contracts.  Each exception
-- is its own function, answering "is the contract within this exception?"; section 5(1) and (2) then take the three
-- answers as yes/no inputs (a caller passes `... EQUALS JUST TRUE`): a contract that no stated exception reaches is
-- caught by the general rule.  The prescribed qualifications, proceedings and activities the Act leaves to the Minister
-- are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs: NOTHING there means "not known" and the answer follows it.

§ `Section 5(3A) to (3E) -- the contracts to which subsections (1) and (2) do not apply`

-- src:447 | (3A) Subsections (1) and (2) shall not apply to —
-- src:449 | (a) a contract for gaming that is conducted under the control or
-- src:450 | supervision of a person or an organisation that is exempted
-- src:451 | under section 24 of the repealed Common Gaming Houses
-- src:452 | Act 1961 from the provisions of that Act in respect of such
-- src:453 | gaming;
-- src:512 | (3B) In the case of a person or an organisation exempted under
-- src:513 | section 24 of the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961 in
-- src:514 | respect of any gaming conducted for or on behalf of another person or
-- src:515 | organisation, subsection (3A)(a) applies only if the contract is for
-- src:520 | gaming conducted by that person or organisation for or on behalf of
-- src:521 | that other person or organisation.
-- src:527 | (3C) Subsection (3A)(a) shall not apply to any gaming conducted
-- src:528 | in premises owned or used by a private body exempted under the
-- src:529 | repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961.
@ref s 5(3A)(a), (3B), (3C) (src:447-529)
GIVEN `the gaming is conducted under the control or supervision of a person or organisation exempted under section 24 of the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gaming is conducted for or on behalf of another person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for gaming conducted by the exempted person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gaming is conducted in premises owned or used by a private body exempted under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3A)(a) with (3B) and (3C) the contract for gaming under an exempted person's control is within the exception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the gaming is conducted under the control or supervision of a person or organisation exempted under section 24 of the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract for gaming that is conducted under the control or supervision of a person or an organisation that is exempted under section 24"
        IF `the gaming is conducted in premises owned or used by a private body exempted under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3A)(a) shall not apply to any gaming conducted in premises owned or used by a private body exempted"
        IF `the gaming is conducted for or on behalf of another person or organisation` AND (NOT `the contract is for gaming conducted by the exempted person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (3A)(a) applies only if the contract is for gaming conducted by that person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:457 | (b) a contract for betting that is held, promoted, organised,
-- src:458 | administered or operated by a person or an organisation
-- src:459 | that is exempted under section 22 of the repealed Betting
-- src:460 | Act 1960 from the provisions of that Act in respect of such
-- src:461 | betting, only if the betting takes place under the control or
-- src:462 | supervision of that person or organisation;
-- src:535 | (3D) In the case of a person or an organisation exempted under
-- src:536 | section 22 of the repealed Betting Act 1960 in respect of any betting
-- src:537 | held, promoted, organised, administered or operated for or on behalf
-- src:538 | of another person or organisation, subsection (3A)(b) applies only if
-- src:539 | the contract is for betting held, promoted, organised, administered or
-- src:540 | operated by that person or organisation for or on behalf of that other
-- src:541 | person or organisation.
@ref s 5(3A)(b) and (3D) (src:457-541)
GIVEN `the betting is held promoted organised administered or operated by a person or organisation exempted under section 22 of the repealed Betting Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the betting takes place under the control or supervision of that person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the betting is held promoted organised administered or operated for or on behalf of another person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for betting held promoted organised administered or operated by the exempted person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3A)(b) with (3D) the contract for betting by an exempted person is within the exception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the betting is held promoted organised administered or operated by a person or organisation exempted under section 22 of the repealed Betting Act 1960` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract for betting that is held, promoted, organised, administered or operated by a person or an organisation that is exempted under section 22"
        IF NOT `the betting takes place under the control or supervision of that person or organisation` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if the betting takes place under the control or supervision of that person or organisation"
        IF `the betting is held promoted organised administered or operated for or on behalf of another person or organisation` AND (NOT `the contract is for betting held promoted organised administered or operated by the exempted person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (3A)(b) applies only if the contract is for betting held, promoted, organised, administered or operated by that person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:469 | (ba) a contract by way of gaming, wagering or betting using
-- src:470 | remote communication that is conducted, promoted,
-- src:471 | organised or administered by —
-- src:473 | (i) an exempt operator within the meaning of the
-- src:474 | repealed Remote Gambling Act 2014; or
-- src:478 | (ii) a person that is exempted under section 40 of that Act
-- src:479 | from section 10 or 11 of that Act;
-- src:547 | (3DA) In the case of an exempt operator or person exempted under
-- src:548 | section 40 of the repealed Remote Gambling Act 2014 in respect of
-- src:549 | any gaming, wagering or betting conducted, promoted, organised or
-- src:550 | administered for or on behalf of another person or organisation,
-- src:551 | subsection (3A)(ba) applies only if the contract is for betting
-- src:552 | conducted, promoted, organised or administered by that person or
-- src:553 | organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation.
@ref s 5(3A)(ba) and (3DA) (src:469-553)
GIVEN `the contract is by way of gaming wagering or betting using remote communication conducted promoted organised or administered by an exempt operator or a person exempted under section 40 of the repealed Remote Gambling Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gaming wagering or betting is conducted promoted organised or administered for or on behalf of another person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for betting conducted promoted organised or administered by the exempt operator or exempted person for or on behalf of that other person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3A)(ba) with (3DA) the contract for remote gaming or betting by an exempt operator is within the exception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contract is by way of gaming wagering or betting using remote communication conducted promoted organised or administered by an exempt operator or a person exempted under section 40 of the repealed Remote Gambling Act 2014` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract by way of gaming, wagering or betting using remote communication that is conducted, promoted, organised or administered by an exempt operator ... or a person that is exempted under section 40"
        IF `the gaming wagering or betting is conducted promoted organised or administered for or on behalf of another person or organisation` AND (NOT `the contract is for betting conducted promoted organised or administered by the exempt operator or exempted person for or on behalf of that other person or organisation`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (3A)(ba) applies only if the contract is for betting conducted, promoted, organised or administered by that person or organisation for or on behalf of that other person or organisation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:481 | (c) a contract for betting that takes place on a totalisator
-- src:482 | conducted by or on behalf of the Singapore Totalisator
-- src:483 | Board or a turf club in accordance with an approved
