@ref s 5(3A)(d) (src:488-490)
GIVEN `the contract is to participate in a private lottery promoted or conducted by the holder of a permit granted under section 8 of the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3A)(d) the contract to participate in a private lottery is within the exception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is to participate in a private lottery promoted or conducted by the holder of a permit granted under section 8 of the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract to participate in a private lottery promoted or conducted by the holder of a permit granted under section 8"

-- src:496 | (e) a contract by way of gaming, wagering or betting that is
-- src:497 | conducted, promoted, organised or administered by —
-- src:499 | (i) a licensee or class licensee within the meaning of the
-- src:500 | Gambling Control Act 2022;
-- src:502 | (ii) a person mentioned in section 18(1)(d) or (f) of the
-- src:503 | Gambling Control Act 2022 in the circumstances
-- src:504 | described in that section; or
-- src:506 | (iii) a person who is exempted under section 128 of the
-- src:507 | Gambling Control Act 2022 from section 18 of that
-- src:508 | Act.
@ref s 5(3A)(e) (src:496-508)
GIVEN `the contract is by way of gaming wagering or betting conducted promoted organised or administered by a licensee or class licensee within the meaning of the Gambling Control Act 2022 or by a person mentioned in section 18(1)(d) or (f) of that Act in the circumstances described there or by a person exempted under section 128 of that Act from section 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3A)(e) the contract for gaming wagering or betting under the Gambling Control Act 2022 is within the exception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is by way of gaming wagering or betting conducted promoted organised or administered by a licensee or class licensee within the meaning of the Gambling Control Act 2022 or by a person mentioned in section 18(1)(d) or (f) of that Act in the circumstances described there or by a person exempted under section 128 of that Act from section 18` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract by way of gaming, wagering or betting that is conducted, promoted, organised or administered by — (i) a licensee or class licensee ...; (ii) ...; or (iii) ..."

-- src:559 | (3E) In subsection (3A) —
-- src:561 | “contract” excludes a contract for or which involves —
-- src:563 | (a) the lending of any money or other valuable thing for
-- src:564 | such gaming or wagering;
-- src:566 | (b) the extension of any form of credit for such gaming or
-- src:567 | wagering; or
-- src:569 | (c) the giving of security in respect of the act referred to
-- src:570 | in paragraph (a) or (b);
@ref s 5(3E) "contract" excludes (src:559-570)
GIVEN `the contract involves the lending of money or other valuable thing for the gaming or wagering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract involves the extension of a form of credit for the gaming or wagering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract involves the giving of security in respect of such lending or extension of credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3E) the contract is a contract within subsection (3A)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract involves the lending of money or other valuable thing for the gaming or wagering` OR `the contract involves the extension of a form of credit for the gaming or wagering` OR `the contract involves the giving of security in respect of such lending or extension of credit` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“contract” excludes a contract for or which involves — (a) the lending of any money or other valuable thing for such gaming or wagering; (b) the extension of any form of credit ...; or (c) the giving of security"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "excludes" names what is not a "contract"; it does not say that every other contract is one

-- src:575 | “private body” has the same meaning as in any notification made
-- src:576 | under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961 which
-- src:577 | exempts gaming conducted in premises owned or used by a
-- src:578 | private body;
@ref s 5(3E) "private body" (src:575-578)
GIVEN `the body is a private body under a notification made under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961 which exempts gaming conducted in premises owned or used by a private body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3E) the body is a private body` MEANS
    `the body is a private body under a notification made under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961 which exempts gaming conducted in premises owned or used by a private body` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in any notification made under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961"

-- src:582 | “private lottery” has the same meaning as in the repealed Private
-- src:583 | Lotteries Act 2011;
@ref s 5(3E) "private lottery" (src:582-583)
GIVEN `the activity is a private lottery within the meaning of the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3E) the activity is a private lottery` MEANS
    `the activity is a private lottery within the meaning of the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011"

-- src:587 | “totalisator”, “Singapore Totalisator Board”, “turf club” and
-- src:588 | “approved scheme” have the same meanings as in the
-- src:589 | Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987.
@ref s 5(3E) "totalisator" and related terms (src:587-589)
GIVEN `the thing is a totalisator or the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club or an approved scheme within the meaning of the Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3E) the thing is a totalisator or the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club or an approved scheme` MEANS
    `the thing is a totalisator or the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club or an approved scheme within the meaning of the Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "have the same meanings as in the Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987"

§ `Section 5(3) and (4) -- other exceptions; Section 5(5) -- investment activity`

-- src:442 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) shall not be deemed to apply to any
-- src:443 | subscription or contribution, or agreement to subscribe or contribute,
-- src:444 | for or toward any plate, prize or sum of money to be awarded to the
-- src:445 | winner or winners of any lawful game, sport, pastime or exercise.
@ref s 5(3) (src:442-445)
GIVEN `the contract is a subscription or contribution or an agreement to subscribe or contribute for or toward a plate prize or sum of money to be awarded to the winner or winners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the game sport pastime or exercise is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3) the subscription or contribution is within the exception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is a subscription or contribution or an agreement to subscribe or contribute for or toward a plate prize or sum of money to be awarded to the winner or winners` AND `the game sport pastime or exercise is lawful` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any subscription or contribution, or agreement to subscribe or contribute, for or toward any plate, prize or sum of money to be awarded to the winner or winners of any lawful game, sport, pastime or exercise"

-- src:642 | (i) such other activity as the Minister may by notification
-- src:643 | prescribe.
@ref s 5(5)(i) (src:642-643)
GIVEN `the Minister has prescribed the activity by notification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(5)(i) the activity is one that the Minister has prescribed by notification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Minister has prescribed the activity by notification`
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“investment activity” means any of the following activities"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(i) such other activity as the Minister may by notification prescribe"

-- src:598 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), “investment activity” means
-- src:599 | any of the following activities:
-- src:601 | (a) a transaction in relation to a contract or an option for the
-- src:602 | future delivery of any securities, commodity, currency or
-- src:603 | financial instrument, whether or not there is any intention
-- src:604 | of actual delivery of such securities, commodity, currency
-- src:605 | or financial instrument;
-- src:607 | (b) a transaction in relation to a contract or an option which is
-- src:608 | entered into with the intention of settlement of differences
-- src:609 | in the prices or values of any securities, commodity,
-- src:610 | currency or financial instrument, whether or not there is
-- src:611 | any intention of actual delivery of such securities,
-- src:612 | commodity, currency or financial instrument;
-- src:614 | (c) a transaction involving the exchange or grant of an option
-- src:615 | for the exchange of any securities, commodity, currency or
-- src:616 | financial instrument;
-- src:618 | (d) a transaction in securities, commodity, currency or
-- src:619 | financial instrument;
-- src:624 | (e) a transaction involving the grant of a right or an option
-- src:625 | relating to an obligation to pay interest or the exchange or
-- src:626 | grant of an option for the exchange of obligations to pay
-- src:627 | interest;
-- src:629 | (f) a transaction in relation to a contract or an option to pay the
-- src:630 | difference between a pre-agreed interest rate and the rate
-- src:631 | prevailing as at specified intervals;
-- src:633 | (g) a transaction in relation to any securities, futures contract
-- src:634 | or derivative which is listed or traded on any stock
-- src:635 | exchange, futures exchange or commodities exchange in
-- src:636 | any country outside Singapore;
-- src:638 | (h) a transaction in relation to any other derivative including
-- src:639 | but not limited to any swap, cap, collar, floor and any
-- src:640 | combination thereof;
@ref s 5(5) (src:598-640)
GIVEN `the kind of activity` IS A `Kind of activity under section 5(5)`
      `the Minister has prescribed the activity by notification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(5) the activity is an investment activity` MEANS
    IF `the kind of activity` EQUALS `Another activity`
    THEN `s 5(5)(i) the activity is one that the Minister has prescribed by notification` `the Minister has prescribed the activity by notification`
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:593 | (4) For the avoidance of doubt, this section shall not affect the
-- src:594 | validity or enforceability of any contract or agreement entered into by
-- src:595 | either or each party by way of business and the making or
-- src:596 | performance of which by any party constitutes an investment activity.
@ref s 5(4) (src:593-596)
GIVEN `the contract was entered into by either or each party by way of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the making or performance of the contract by any party constitutes an investment activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(4) section 5 affects the validity or enforceability of the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract was entered into by either or each party by way of business` AND `the making or performance of the contract by any party constitutes an investment activity` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section shall not affect the validity or enforceability of any contract or agreement entered into by either or each party by way of business and the making or performance of which by any party constitutes an investment activity"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "entered into by either or each party by way of business"

§ `Section 5(1), (2) and (6) -- the nullity, the bar and the promises`

-- src:434 | 5.—(1) All contracts or agreements, whether by parol or in writing,
-- src:435 | by way of gaming or wagering shall be null and void.
@ref s 5(1) (src:434-435)
GIVEN `the contract is by way of gaming or wagering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is within the exception of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is within the exceptions of subsection (3A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is within the saving of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contract is by way of gaming or wagering` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All contracts or agreements, whether by parol or in writing, by way of gaming or wagering"
        IF `the contract is within the exception of subsection (3)` OR `the contract is within the exceptions of subsection (3A)` OR `the contract is within the saving of subsection (4)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) shall not be deemed to apply" / "shall not apply to" -- an exception lifts the deeming
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:437 | (2) No action shall be brought or maintained in the court for
-- src:438 | recovering any sum of money or valuable thing alleged to be won
-- src:439 | upon any wager or which has been deposited in the hands of any
-- src:440 | person to abide the event on which any wager has been made.
@ref s 5(2) (src:437-440)
GIVEN `the sum or thing is alleged to be won upon a wager or has been deposited in the hands of a person to abide the event on which a wager has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is within the exception of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is within the exceptions of subsection (3A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is within the saving of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) an action may be brought or maintained in the court for recovering the sum or thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the sum or thing is alleged to be won upon a wager or has been deposited in the hands of a person to abide the event on which a wager has been made` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any sum of money or valuable thing alleged to be won upon any wager or which has been deposited in the hands of any person to abide the event on which any wager has been made"
        IF `the contract is within the exception of subsection (3)` OR `the contract is within the exceptions of subsection (3A)` OR `the contract is within the saving of subsection (4)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (1) and (2) shall not apply" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No action shall be brought or maintained in the court for recovering any sum of money or valuable thing alleged to be won upon any wager"

-- src:648 | (6) Any promise, express or implied, to pay any person any sum of
-- src:649 | money paid by him under or in respect of any contract or agreement
-- src:650 | rendered null and void by subsections (1) and (2), or to pay any sum
-- src:651 | of money by way of commission, fee, reward or otherwise in respect
-- src:652 | of any such contract or of any services in relation thereto or in
-- src:653 | connection therewith, shall be null and void, and no action shall be
-- src:654 | brought or maintained to recover any such sum of money.
@ref s 5(6) (src:648-654)
GIVEN `the promise is to pay a sum of money paid under or in respect of a contract or agreement rendered null and void by subsections (1) and (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promise is to pay a sum of money by way of commission fee reward or otherwise in respect of such a contract or of services in relation to or in connection with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(6) the promise express or implied is null and void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the promise is to pay a sum of money paid under or in respect of a contract or agreement rendered null and void by subsections (1) and (2)` OR `the promise is to pay a sum of money by way of commission fee reward or otherwise in respect of such a contract or of services in relation to or in connection with it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any promise, express or implied, to pay any person any sum of money paid by him under or in respect of any contract ... rendered null and void by subsections (1) and (2), or to pay any sum of money by way of commission, fee, reward or otherwise"

-- src:653 | connection therewith, shall be null and void, and no action shall be
-- src:654 | brought or maintained to recover any such sum of money.
@ref s 5(6) no action to recover (src:653-654)
GIVEN `the promise is to pay a sum of money paid under or in respect of a contract or agreement rendered null and void by subsections (1) and (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promise is to pay a sum of money by way of commission fee reward or otherwise in respect of such a contract or of services in relation to or in connection with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(6) an action may be brought or maintained to recover the sum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the promise is to pay a sum of money paid under or in respect of a contract or agreement rendered null and void by subsections (1) and (2)` OR `the promise is to pay a sum of money by way of commission fee reward or otherwise in respect of such a contract or of services in relation to or in connection with it` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no action shall be brought or maintained to recover any such sum of money"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such sum of money"

§ `Section 5A -- maintenance and champerty`

-- src:658 | 5A.—(1) It is declared that no person is, under the law of
-- src:659 | Singapore, liable in tort for any conduct on account of its being
-- src:660 | maintenance or champerty as known to the common law.
@ref s 5A(1) (src:658-660)
GIVEN `the liability in tort asserted rests only on the conduct being maintenance or champerty as known to the common law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A(1) the person is liable in tort for the conduct on account of its being maintenance or champerty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the liability in tort asserted rests only on the conduct being maintenance or champerty as known to the common law` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person is, under the law of Singapore, liable in tort for any conduct on account of its being maintenance or champerty"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on account of its being maintenance or champerty as known to the common law" -- liability in tort on another footing is not addressed

-- src:664 | (2) Subject to section 5B, the abolition of civil liability under the
-- src:665 | law of Singapore for maintenance and champerty does not affect any
-- src:670 | rule of that law as to the cases in which a contract is to be treated as
-- src:671 | contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal.
@ref s 5A(2) (src:664-671)
GIVEN `section 5B applies to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A(2) the abolition of civil liability affects the rule as to when a contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 5B applies to the contract` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 5B"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the abolition of civil liability under the law of Singapore for maintenance and champerty does not affect any rule of that law as to the cases in which a contract is to be treated as contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal"

§ `Section 5B -- contracts for funding of claims`

-- src:677 | 5B.—(1) This section applies only in relation to prescribed dispute
-- src:678 | resolution proceedings.
@ref s 5B(1) (src:677-678)
GIVEN `the proceedings are prescribed dispute resolution proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(1) section 5B applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proceedings are prescribed dispute resolution proceedings`
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only in relation to prescribed dispute resolution proceedings"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed" -- the class of proceedings is set by regulations under subsection (8)

-- src:682 | (2) A contract under which a qualifying Third‑Party Funder
-- src:683 | provides funds to any party for the purpose of funding all or part
-- src:684 | of the costs of that party in prescribed dispute resolution proceedings
-- src:685 | is not contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is
-- src:686 | a contract for maintenance or champerty.
@ref s 5B(2) (src:682-686)
GIVEN `a qualifying Third-Party Funder provides funds to a party for the purpose of funding all or part of the costs of that party in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are prescribed dispute resolution proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(2) the funding contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is a contract for maintenance or champerty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a qualifying Third-Party Funder provides funds to a party for the purpose of funding all or part of the costs of that party in the proceedings` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A contract under which a qualifying Third-Party Funder provides funds to any party for the purpose of funding all or part of the costs of that party"
        IF `the proceedings are prescribed dispute resolution proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is a contract for maintenance or champerty"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed dispute resolution proceedings"

-- src:690 | (3) Every qualifying Third‑Party Funder and funded party must, in
-- src:691 | relation to a third‑party funding contract, comply with and ensure that
-- src:692 | such requirements as may be prescribed under subsection (8) are
-- src:693 | complied with.
@ref s 5B(3) (src:690-693)
GIVEN `the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party in relation to a third-party funding contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(3) the duty to comply with the prescribed requirements arises` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party in relation to a third-party funding contract` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every qualifying Third-Party Funder and funded party must, in relation to a third-party funding contract" -- the duty does not arise for anyone else (fork QD)

@ref s 5B(3) compliance (src:690-693)
GIVEN `the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party in relation to a third-party funding contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(3) the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party in relation to a third-party funding contract` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a third-party funding contract" -- the duty does not arise; the companion s 5B(3) the duty to comply with the prescribed requirements arises answers that (fork QD)
        IF `the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (fork QB); subsection (4) says what follows for a funder that fails to comply

@ref s 5B(3) as a regulative rule (src:690-693)
GIVEN party IS A `Party under section 5B(3)`
      `the duty arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under section 5B(3)` `Act under section 5B(3)`
`s 5B(3) the qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party must comply with the prescribed requirements` MEANS
    IF `the duty arises`
    THEN
        PARTY party
        MUST `comply with the requirements prescribed for the third-party funding contract and ensure that they are complied with`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY party BECAUSE "prescribed requirement for the third-party funding contract not complied with (s 5B(3))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:697 | (4) Where a Third‑Party Funder —
-- src:699 | (a) ceases to be a qualifying Third‑Party Funder; or
-- src:701 | (b) fails to comply with any prescribed requirement mentioned
-- src:702 | in subsection (3),
-- src:704 | the rights of the Third‑Party Funder under or arising out of the
-- src:705 | third‑party funding contract affected by or connected with the
-- src:706 | disqualification or non‑compliance are not enforceable by action or
-- src:707 | other legal proceedings, including arbitration proceedings.
@ref s 5B(4) (src:697-707)
GIVEN `the Third-Party Funder has ceased to be a qualifying Third-Party Funder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Third-Party Funder has failed to comply with a prescribed requirement mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is under or arises out of the third-party funding contract affected by or connected with the disqualification or non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relief against the disability has been granted under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Third-Party Funder has ceased to be a qualifying Third-Party Funder` OR `the Third-Party Funder has failed to comply with a prescribed requirement mentioned in subsection (3)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a Third-Party Funder — (a) ceases to be a qualifying Third-Party Funder; or (b) fails to comply" -- the bar does not arise
        IF NOT `the right is under or arises out of the third-party funding contract affected by or connected with the disqualification or non-compliance` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rights of the Third-Party Funder under or arising out of the third-party funding contract affected by or connected with the disqualification or non-compliance"
        IF `relief against the disability has been granted under subsection (6)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsections (5) and (6) let the court or tribunal grant relief against the disability; a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not enforceable by action or other legal proceedings, including arbitration proceedings"

-- src:711 | (5) A Third‑Party Funder may apply to the court or arbitral tribunal
-- src:712 | for relief against the disability imposed by subsection (4).
@ref s 5B(5) (src:711-712)
GIVEN `the disability imposed by subsection (4) applies to the Third-Party Funder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(5) the Third-Party Funder may apply to the court or arbitral tribunal for relief against the disability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disability imposed by subsection (4) applies to the Third-Party Funder` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relief against the disability imposed by subsection (4)"

-- src:716 | (6) The court or arbitral tribunal, on being satisfied —
-- src:718 | (a) that the disqualification or non‑compliance was accidental
-- src:719 | or due to inadvertence or some other sufficient cause; or
-- src:721 | (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief,
-- src:726 | may grant such relief either generally, or as respects any third‑party
-- src:727 | funding contract, on such conditions (if any) as the court or arbitral
-- src:728 | tribunal may impose, including (but not limited to) a condition that
-- src:729 | the costs of the application be paid by the Third‑Party Funder.
@ref s 5B(6) (src:716-729)
GIVEN `the disqualification or non-compliance was accidental or due to inadvertence or some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may grant relief` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disqualification or non-compliance was accidental or due to inadvertence or some other sufficient cause` OR `on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on being satisfied — (a) that the disqualification or non-compliance was accidental or due to inadvertence or some other sufficient cause; or (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief" -- MARGINAL (b): "on being satisfied" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling)

-- src:733 | (7) Subsection (4) does not prejudice the rights of any other party as
-- src:734 | against the Third‑Party Funder in respect of a third‑party funding
-- src:735 | contract.
@ref s 5B(7) (src:733-735)
GIVEN `the right is that of a party other than the Third-Party Funder as against the Third-Party Funder in respect of the third-party funding contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(7) subsection (4) prejudices the rights of the other party as against the Third-Party Funder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the right is that of a party other than the Third-Party Funder as against the Third-Party Funder in respect of the third-party funding contract` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not prejudice the rights of any other party as against the Third-Party Funder"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rights of any other party as against the Third-Party Funder in respect of a third-party funding contract"

-- src:756 | (9) Any addition, deletion or other variation to the qualifications
-- src:757 | and other requirements of a Third‑Party Funder or the class or classes
-- src:758 | or description of dispute resolution proceedings prescribed under
-- src:759 | subsection (8) does not affect any contract which was entered into
-- src:760 | before the date of commencement of that addition, deletion or
-- src:761 | variation.
@ref s 5B(9) (src:756-761)
GIVEN `the contract was entered into before the date of commencement of the addition deletion or variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(9) a later addition deletion or variation of the qualifications requirements or class of proceedings affects the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract was entered into before the date of commencement of the addition deletion or variation` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect any contract which was entered into before the date of commencement of that addition, deletion or variation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of a contract entered into on or after that date

§ `Section 5B(10) -- definitions`

-- src:765 | (10) In this section, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:767 | “arbitral tribunal” or “court” means any arbitral tribunal or court
-- src:768 | before which proceedings to enforce a right referred to in
-- src:769 | subsection (4) are commenced or before which an issue
-- src:770 | relating to subsection (4) arises;
@ref s 5B(10) "arbitral tribunal" or "court" (src:765-770)
GIVEN `the body is an arbitral tribunal or court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings to enforce a right referred to in subsection (4) are commenced before it or an issue relating to subsection (4) arises before it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(10) the body is the arbitral tribunal or court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the body is an arbitral tribunal or court` AND `proceedings to enforce a right referred to in subsection (4) are commenced before it or an issue relating to subsection (4) arises before it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“arbitral tribunal” or “court” means any arbitral tribunal or court before which proceedings to enforce a right referred to in subsection (4) are commenced"

-- src:765 | (10) In this section, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:772 | “dispute resolution proceedings” means the entire process of
-- src:773 | resolving or attempting to resolve a dispute between 2 or
-- src:778 | more parties and includes any civil, mediation, conciliation,
-- src:779 | arbitration or insolvency proceedings;
@ref s 5B(10) "dispute resolution proceedings" (src:765-779)
GIVEN `the process is the entire process of resolving or attempting to resolve a dispute between 2 or more parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process is civil mediation conciliation arbitration or insolvency proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(10) the process is dispute resolution proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the process is the entire process of resolving or attempting to resolve a dispute between 2 or more parties` OR `the process is civil mediation conciliation arbitration or insolvency proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“dispute resolution proceedings” means the entire process of resolving or attempting to resolve a dispute between 2 or more parties" -- "means ... and includes" is read as closing the class at the two limbs (fork F-D1)

-- src:765 | (10) In this section, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:781 | “funded party” means a party to dispute resolution proceedings
-- src:782 | who enters into an agreement with a Third‑Party Funder for
-- src:783 | the funding of all or part of the costs of the proceedings and
-- src:784 | includes a liquidator or judicial manager;
@ref s 5B(10) "funded party" (src:765-784)
GIVEN `the person is a party to dispute resolution proceedings who enters into an agreement with a Third-Party Funder for the funding of all or part of the costs of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a liquidator or judicial manager` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(10) the person is a funded party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the person is a party to dispute resolution proceedings who enters into an agreement with a Third-Party Funder for the funding of all or part of the costs of the proceedings` OR `the person is a liquidator or judicial manager` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“funded party” means a party to dispute resolution proceedings who enters into an agreement with a Third-Party Funder" -- fork F-D1

-- src:765 | (10) In this section, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:786 | “qualifying Third‑Party Funder” means a Third‑Party Funder
-- src:787 | who satisfies and continues to satisfy such qualifications and
-- src:788 | other requirements as may be prescribed;
@ref s 5B(10) "qualifying Third-Party Funder" (src:765-788)
GIVEN `the person is a Third-Party Funder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies and continues to satisfy the qualifications and other requirements that are prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(10) the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF NOT `the person is a Third-Party Funder` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying Third-Party Funder” means a Third-Party Funder who satisfies and continues to satisfy such qualifications"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the person satisfies and continues to satisfy the qualifications and other requirements that are prescribed`
            WHEN JUST x THEN
                IF x THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who satisfies and continues to satisfy such qualifications and other requirements as may be prescribed"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as may be prescribed" -- the qualifications are set by regulations under subsection (8)(a)

-- src:765 | (10) In this section, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:790 | “Third‑Party Funder” means a person who carries on the
-- src:791 | business of funding all or part of the costs of dispute
-- src:792 | resolution proceedings to which the person is not a party;
@ref s 5B(10) "Third-Party Funder" (src:765-792)
GIVEN `the person carries on the business of funding all or part of the costs of dispute resolution proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(10) the person is a Third-Party Funder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the person carries on the business of funding all or part of the costs of dispute resolution proceedings` AND (NOT `the person is a party to those proceedings`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Third-Party Funder” means a person who carries on the business of funding all or part of the costs of dispute resolution proceedings to which the person is not a party"

-- src:765 | (10) In this section, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:794 | “third‑party funding contract” means a contract or agreement by
-- src:795 | a party or potential party to dispute resolution proceedings
-- src:796 | with a Third‑Party Funder for the funding of all or part of the
-- src:797 | costs of the proceedings in return for a share or other interest
-- src:798 | in the proceeds or potential proceeds of the proceedings to
-- src:799 | which the party or potential party may become entitled.
@ref s 5B(10) "third-party funding contract" (src:765-799)
GIVEN `the contract is by a party or potential party to dispute resolution proceedings with a Third-Party Funder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the funding of all or part of the costs of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the funding is in return for a share or other interest in the proceeds or potential proceeds to which the party or potential party may become entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B(10) the contract is a third-party funding contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the contract is by a party or potential party to dispute resolution proceedings with a Third-Party Funder` AND `the contract is for the funding of all or part of the costs of the proceedings` AND `the funding is in return for a share or other interest in the proceeds or potential proceeds to which the party or potential party may become entitled` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“third-party funding contract” means a contract or agreement by a party or potential party to dispute resolution proceedings with a Third-Party Funder for the funding of all or part of the costs of the proceedings in return for a share or other interest"

§§ `Sections 5, 5A and 5B -- tests`

-- s 5(3A)(a), (3B), (3C)
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(a) with (3B) and (3C) the contract for gaming under an exempted person's control is within the exception` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- gaming under the control of an exempted person
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(a) with (3B) and (3C) the contract for gaming under an exempted person's control is within the exception` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- conducted for another and the contract is for gaming by the exempted person for that other: (3B) is met
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(a) with (3B) and (3C) the contract for gaming under an exempted person's control is within the exception` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (3B) "applies only if" fails
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(a) with (3B) and (3C) the contract for gaming under an exempted person's control is within the exception` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (3C) premises of a private body: "shall not apply"
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(a) with (3B) and (3C) the contract for gaming under an exempted person's control is within the exception` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not gaming under an exempted person's control
-- s 5(3A)(b), (3D)
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(b) with (3D) the contract for betting by an exempted person is within the exception` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- betting under the exempted person's control
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(b) with (3D) the contract for betting by an exempted person is within the exception` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "only if the betting takes place under the control or supervision of that person"
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(b) with (3D) the contract for betting by an exempted person is within the exception` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- for another, and the contract is for betting by that person for that other: (3D) is met
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(b) with (3D) the contract for betting by an exempted person is within the exception` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (3D) "applies only if" fails
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(b) with (3D) the contract for betting by an exempted person is within the exception` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not betting by an exempted person
-- s 5(3A)(ba), (3DA)
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(ba) with (3DA) the contract for remote gaming or betting by an exempt operator is within the exception` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- remote betting by an exempt operator
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(ba) with (3DA) the contract for remote gaming or betting by an exempt operator is within the exception` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- for another, and the contract is not for betting by the exempt operator for that other: (3DA)
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(ba) with (3DA) the contract for remote gaming or betting by an exempt operator is within the exception` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (3DA) met
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(ba) with (3DA) the contract for remote gaming or betting by an exempt operator is within the exception` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not remote gaming by an exempt operator
-- s 5(3A)(c), (d), (e)
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(c) the contract for betting on a totalisator is within the exception` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a totalisator bet
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(c) the contract for betting on a totalisator is within the exception` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a totalisator bet
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(d) the contract to participate in a private lottery is within the exception` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a permitted private lottery
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(d) the contract to participate in a private lottery is within the exception` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a permitted private lottery
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(e) the contract for gaming wagering or betting under the Gambling Control Act 2022 is within the exception` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a licensee's contract
#ASSERT `s 5(3A)(e) the contract for gaming wagering or betting under the Gambling Control Act 2022 is within the exception` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a licensee's or exempted person's contract
-- s 5(3E)
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the contract is a contract within subsection (3A)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "excludes a contract for or which involves the lending of any money"
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the contract is a contract within subsection (3A)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "the extension of any form of credit"
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the contract is a contract within subsection (3A)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "the giving of security"
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the contract is a contract within subsection (3A)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "excludes" does not say every other contract is one
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the body is a private body` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the notification's meaning is the input
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the body is a private body` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- the notification is not among the sources
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the activity is a private lottery` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the repealed Act's meaning is the input
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the activity is a private lottery` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011 is not among the sources
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the thing is a totalisator or the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club or an approved scheme` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987's meaning is the input
#ASSERT `s 5(3E) the thing is a totalisator or the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club or an approved scheme` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- not among the sources
-- s 5(3)
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the subscription or contribution is within the exception` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a subscription for a prize of a lawful game
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the subscription or contribution is within the exception` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the game is not lawful: "any lawful game"
#ASSERT `s 5(3) the subscription or contribution is within the exception` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a subscription for a prize
-- s 5(5)
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the activity is an investment activity` `Contract or option for the future delivery of securities commodity currency or a financial instrument` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- head (a)
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the activity is an investment activity` `Any other derivative including a swap cap collar or floor` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- head (h)
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the activity is an investment activity` `Another activity` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- head (i): the Minister has prescribed it
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the activity is an investment activity` `Another activity` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not prescribed: "means any of the following activities"
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the activity is an investment activity` `Another activity` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the Minister has prescribed it is not known
-- s 5(4)
#ASSERT `s 5(4) section 5 affects the validity or enforceability of the contract` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not affect the validity or enforceability"
#ASSERT `s 5(4) section 5 affects the validity or enforceability of the contract` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an investment activity
#ASSERT `s 5(4) section 5 affects the validity or enforceability of the contract` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entered into by way of business
-- s 5(1), (2), (6)
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be null and void"
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- within the exception of (3)
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- within an exception of (3A)
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- within the saving of (4)
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not by way of gaming or wagering
#ASSERT `s 5(2) an action may be brought or maintained in the court for recovering the sum or thing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "No action shall be brought or maintained"
#ASSERT `s 5(2) an action may be brought or maintained in the court for recovering the sum or thing` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an exception of (3A) lifts the bar and grants nothing
#ASSERT `s 5(2) an action may be brought or maintained in the court for recovering the sum or thing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a sum won on a wager or deposited with a stakeholder
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the promise express or implied is null and void` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a promise to repay a sum paid under a void wager
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the promise express or implied is null and void` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a promise of commission in respect of such a contract
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the promise express or implied is null and void` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another promise
#ASSERT `s 5(6) an action may be brought or maintained to recover the sum` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "no action shall be brought or maintained to recover any such sum"
#ASSERT `s 5(6) an action may be brought or maintained to recover the sum` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another sum
-- s 5A
#ASSERT `s 5A(1) the person is liable in tort for the conduct on account of its being maintenance or champerty` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "no person is ... liable in tort"
#ASSERT `s 5A(1) the person is liable in tort for the conduct on account of its being maintenance or champerty` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- liability on another footing
#ASSERT `s 5A(2) the abolition of civil liability affects the rule as to when a contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not affect any rule"
#ASSERT `s 5A(2) the abolition of civil liability affects the rule as to when a contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "Subject to section 5B"
-- s 5B
#ASSERT `s 5B(1) section 5B applies` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- prescribed proceedings
#ASSERT `s 5B(1) section 5B applies` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "applies only in relation to prescribed dispute resolution proceedings"
#ASSERT `s 5B(1) section 5B applies` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the proceedings are prescribed is not known
#ASSERT `s 5B(2) the funding contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is a contract for maintenance or champerty` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "is not contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal"
#ASSERT `s 5B(2) the funding contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is a contract for maintenance or champerty` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- not in prescribed proceedings
#ASSERT `s 5B(2) the funding contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is a contract for maintenance or champerty` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- no qualifying funder funding a party's costs
#ASSERT `s 5B(3) the duty to comply with the prescribed requirements arises` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "Every qualifying Third-Party Funder and funded party must"
#ASSERT `s 5B(3) the duty to comply with the prescribed requirements arises` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- anyone else
#ASSERT `s 5B(3) the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- complied
#ASSERT `s 5B(3) the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not complied: a bare "must" (QB); subsection (4) says what follows
#ASSERT `s 5B(3) the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the duty does not arise: see the companion
-- The duty as a regulative rule: complying fulfils it; not complying is a breach; no duty is fulfilled.
#TRACE `s 5B(3) the qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party must comply with the prescribed requirements` `The qualifying Third-Party Funder` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The qualifying Third-Party Funder` DOES `comply with the requirements prescribed for the third-party funding contract and ensure that they are complied with` AT 3
#TRACE `s 5B(3) the qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party must comply with the prescribed requirements` `The funded party` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
#TRACE `s 5B(3) the qualifying Third-Party Funder or the funded party must comply with the prescribed requirements` `The funded party` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
#ASSERT `s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- ceased to be qualifying: "are not enforceable"
#ASSERT `s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- failed to comply with a prescribed requirement
#ASSERT `s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- relief granted under (6): a lifted bar grants nothing
#ASSERT `s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a right not connected with the non-compliance
#ASSERT `s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- neither (a) nor (b)
#ASSERT `s 5B(5) the Third-Party Funder may apply to the court or arbitral tribunal for relief against the disability` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may apply"
#ASSERT `s 5B(5) the Third-Party Funder may apply to the court or arbitral tribunal for relief against the disability` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no disability under (4)
#ASSERT `s 5B(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may grant relief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) accidental or inadvertent
#ASSERT `s 5B(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may grant relief` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) just and equitable
#ASSERT `s 5B(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may grant relief` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not satisfied of (a) or (b): "on being satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 5B(7) subsection (4) prejudices the rights of the other party as against the Third-Party Funder` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not prejudice the rights of any other party"
#ASSERT `s 5B(7) subsection (4) prejudices the rights of the other party as against the Third-Party Funder` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another right
#ASSERT `s 5B(9) a later addition deletion or variation of the qualifications requirements or class of proceedings affects the contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not affect any contract which was entered into before"
#ASSERT `s 5B(9) a later addition deletion or variation of the qualifications requirements or class of proceedings affects the contract` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a contract entered into later: the text is silent
-- s 5B(10)
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the body is the arbitral tribunal or court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a tribunal before which (4) is in issue
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the body is the arbitral tribunal or court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a tribunal before which nothing under (4) arises: "means"
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the body is the arbitral tribunal or court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the context otherwise requires
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the process is dispute resolution proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the entire process of resolving a dispute
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the process is dispute resolution proceedings` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- arbitration is included
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the process is dispute resolution proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither limb (fork F-D1)
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a funded party` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a funded party
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a funded party` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "includes a liquidator or judicial manager"
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a funded party` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither (fork F-D1)
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- satisfies the prescribed qualifications
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- does not satisfy them: "who satisfies and continues to satisfy"
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder` TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the prescribed qualifications are not known
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a qualifying Third-Party Funder` FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a Third-Party Funder at all
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a Third-Party Funder` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- funds the costs of proceedings it is not a party to
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a Third-Party Funder` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a party to the proceedings: "to which the person is not a party"
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the person is a Third-Party Funder` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- does not carry on that business
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the contract is a third-party funding contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all three limbs
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the contract is a third-party funding contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no share of the proceeds: "means"
#ASSERT `s 5B(10) the contract is a third-party funding contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the context otherwise requires
